SUMMARY:Grant Application Deadline: Asian Solidarity and Action Project
DESCRIPTION:Got a project that can spark change in your Asian American community? NC Asian Americans Together (NCAAT) is introducing the Asian Solidarity and Action Project (ASAP). Rooted in the powerful tradition of Asian community care\, ASAP is a 3-month incubator (August–October) designed to fund and fuel community-led initiatives. \nWhether your passion is expanding voter education\, fighting for immigration rights\, improving healthcare access\, or capturing local oral histories\, NCAAT wants to back the issues that matter most to your community. \nEach of the 5 selected projects will receive:\n• A $5\,000 stipend to bring your idea to life\n• Monthly project planning support & 1-on-1 coaching\n• Access to a network of grantees and joint office hours\nWhether you have a brand-new idea or want to expand an existing effort\, you can apply as an individual or a team (ages 18+). \nApplication deadline: July 12\, 2026 \nLearn more here and apply here.
URL:https://resilientdurhamnc.org/event/grant-application-deadline-asian-solidarity-and-action-project/
END:VEVENT
